Reserved concurrency 1 addresses overlap between poller invocations, but AWS writes already sent can outlive an invocation. I also found two points needing closer scrutiny: the live poller timeout is 300 seconds, and the registered latch model records burial when it occurs, before any issuer fetch or durable write.
